@startuml poll-stack
' cumin works - the stack: an implementation issue that starts on a pull request that waits for a Maintainer.
' Document: poll.md, section on the stack.
' Render: run scripts/render-diagrams.sh at the root of the repository.
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif

start
:The only open blocker is in
cumin/status/awaiting-merge-decision,
its pull request has the default branch as base,
and deleteBranchOnMerge is true;
:request the implementation:
the branch starts from the branch of the blocker,
and the pull request has that branch as base;
repeat
  :Checks and the review, as for any pull request
  (a conflict with the base branch:
  request a conflict resolution);
  if (The base pull request of the blocker issue
is closed without a merge, or GitHub closed
the stacked pull request, or the update
left the head without the merge commit?) then (yes)
    #Pink:stop the implementation:
    cumin/status/awaiting-decision and a notification;
    stop
  endif
  if (The base of the pull request is
the default branch, and every blocker is closed?) then (no)
    #LightBlue:wait for the base:
    cumin/status/awaiting-base;
    :The Maintainer merges the base (squash).
    GitHub deletes the branch of the blocker
    and changes the base to the default branch;
    if (The base is still not the default branch
one poll_interval after the merge?) then (yes)
      #Pink:stop the implementation:
      cumin/status/awaiting-decision and a notification;
      stop
    endif
  endif
  backward:update onto the default branch:
  cumin/status/implementing, then the Implementer
  merges the default branch with a merge commit;
repeat while (The head contains the merge commit
of the base pull request?) is (no)
-> yes;
:ask for the merge decision or start the merge,
as for any pull request;
stop
@enduml
